<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices lower at 4th summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices lower at 4th summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH, South Africa 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the fourth summer sale fell slightly, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. There was still very good demand for sale.</p>
<p>Of the 2,741 bales offered 43 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2,300-2,700	(2,350-2,600)</p>
<p>		  medium     1,950-2,302	(1,950-2,400)</p>
<p>		  short	1,702-2,750	(2,200-2,550)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2,450-4,010	(2,500-3,036)</p>
<p>		  medium     2,490-2,702	(2,300-2,452)</p>
<p>		  short	2,492-2,800	(    -    )</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 6,000-11,970     (6,002-12,800)</p>
<p>		  medium     3,850-7,450	(4,240-8,502)</p>
<p>		  short	4,000-4,500	(2,900-4,000)</p>
<p>The fifth sale of the season is scheduled for May 20, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
